<!--
  The two users of the LOCAL docker ClickHouse, as a tier has them: mounted
  into the server's users.d by the development Compose file and by CI. The
  passwords are the ones .env.example carries, and the server listens on
  127.0.0.1 alone; a tier writes the same users from its secrets.

  - `migrator`: `telmoni-server migrate` and `telmoni-server rotate`. It makes the database,
    the tables, the view and the row policies: `tenant_isolation`, `TO ALL
    EXCEPT CURRENT_USER`, does not hold it, and its own, `migrator_reads_all`,
    admits it to every row whatever the server's default, so the view, which
    runs as it, and the nightly purge, which lists its partitions from the
    rows, see every project's. It drops those partitions and rewrites away
    the rows a deleted project left (`ALTER DELETE`). Its rights are named
    one by one, never `ALL ON telemetry.*`: ClickHouse grants `ALL` on the
    name `telemetry` too, and with it the right to alter, drop and act as
    the user `telemetry`.
  - `telemetry`: the module. It writes spans and reads them and their
    totals, and the row policy holds it to the projects each read names;
    it marks a deleted project's rows in both tables (`ALTER DELETE`, which
    a lightweight delete needs), each delete naming its one project. It is
    granted those two tables and nothing else in the database: the view
    reads as its definer, so a grant on it would answer every project's
    totals past the policy, and the rollup is the view's alone to write.

  An edit here lands with a restart of the container.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <users>
        <migrator>
            <password>migrator_dev</password>
            <networks>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
            <profile>default</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT CREATE DATABASE, CREATE TABLE, CREATE VIEW, CREATE ROW POLICY, SELECT, INSERT, ALTER DELETE ON telemetry.*</query>
            </grants>
        </migrator>
        <telemetry>
            <password>telemetry_dev</password>
            <networks>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
            <profile>default</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER DELETE ON telemetry.spans</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, ALTER DELETE ON telemetry.spans_hourly</query>
            </grants>
        </telemetry>
    </users>
</clickhouse>
